B.baM=new A.cN("record",B.kV,"How do I record something?","Press REC, the record key in the bar at the foot of the four main screens: Your music, Open Mic, Messages and Learn. On a wider screen, a tablet held sideways or a computer, the bar has no REC: press New idea instead. On other screens, press More, then Everything else, then Record an idea. It starts a new idea \u2014 no naming, no choosing where it lives. You can do both afterwards, once there is something worth filing.\n\nThe first time, it asks to use the microphone. Then it counts 3, 2, 1 and records; press Start now if you are ready sooner. To record from the tap with no count, press Tools in the recorder and turn off Count in before recording.\n\nPress Stop and save when you have it. It is saved in Ideas at once, and the page shows how long it is, with Hear it, Record again (which keeps this one and starts another) and Throw away (with Undo). Done takes you back to where you were.\n\nOn a phone it works with no signal: the recording is kept on the phone first, and goes into Your music by itself when there is signal. One recording runs for up to 12 minutes, which is as long as a song here can hold, and the recorder says so in the last minute.\n\nIf the idea is words and there is nowhere quiet to sing, press Tools in the recorder and then Write it down. It is also under More on Your music, and under More in Ideas. On a phone what you type is kept on the phone as you type it, and goes into Ideas as a song named from its first line when you press Done, or by itself once there is signal.\n\nTo add a recording to a song you already have, open it and press Record it, the gold at the foot. Once the song has a recording, the same gold says Record a take. On a computer, with a song open beside Your music, the gold button says Record, or New take once the song has a recording; with no song open it says New idea.",B.cAE)
B.ewc=s(["workspace_layers_button","layers_record_button"],t.s)
B.bZl=s(["take","takes","another","add","overdub","layer","part","second","share","shared","song"],t.s)
B.baP=new A.cN("take",B.dR,"How do I add a take to a song?","Open the song and press Record a take, the gold button at the foot (Record it, if the song has no recording yet). Takes opens, counts you in, and records over the song while it plays; press Stop when you are done. To come in partway, tap the song's bar on Takes where you want to start, and press Record from there.\n\nA take stays private to you until you share it. Tap it on Takes, press Tools, and press Share for the one you want the room to hear \u2014 nothing you have not shared is ever audible to anybody, including on the Open Mic. The same Tools takes it back, or takes it off the song.\n\nWith no signal, a take is kept on the phone and shown on Takes as On this phone, not sent yet; tap it for Try again. It goes up by itself when there is signal. If a take sounds late, tap it, press Tools, then Volume and timing, and press Line it up to move it while it plays.",B.bZl)
B.exM=s(["workspace_analyze_button","choose_reference_recording"],t.s)
B.c6Q=s(["chord","chords","sheet","lyrics","words","key","tempo","bpm","transcribe","transcription","tab","analyse","analyze","notation","song"],t.s)
B.ba8=new A.cN("sheet",B.dR,"How do I get the chords and words for my song?","Record something first, then open the song and press Song Sheet, and choose one.\n\nChords is free: the chords and the key, with no words or bar lines. The full analysis also writes down the words you sang and puts the chords over them, finds the tempo and the bars, and names the parts; it uses a credit, takes a few minutes, and keeps going if you leave the screen.",B.c6Q)
B.exq=s(["/settings/what-you-play","account_what_you_play_row","what_you_play_sheet"],t.s)
B.ct5=s(["ukulele","uke","bass","piano","keyboard","left","handed","lefty","shape","shapes","diagram","instrument","nashville","roman","sargam","jianpu","solfege","trumpet","sax","saxophone","horn","transpose","transposing","reading"],t.s)
B.b9L=new A.cN("what-you-play",B.dR,"I play a ukulele, a bass or a piano, not a guitar.","Account \u2192 Music \u2192 What you play and how you read.\n\nPick guitar, ukulele, bass or piano, and left-handed if you read a neck the other way round. Every chord diagram, sheet, chart and printed page follows it from then on. The same question is under any chord diagram and in the tuner, so you can answer it where you are.\n\nThe same screen sets how you read: chords as letters, Nashville numbers or Roman numerals; sung notes as letters, do-re-mi, fixed do, sargam or jianpu; and the written key of a transposing instrument, so a trumpet part reads in B\u266d without you moving every chord in your head.\n\nIt is kept with your account, so a new phone starts where the last one left off, and nobody else can see it \u2014 not your band, not a teacher. A song you have already set differently keeps its own setting.",B.ct5)
B.exx=s(["song_audience_dial"],t.s)
B.c9Z=s(["who","hear","private","privacy","public","visible","audience","secret","safe","sharing","permission","song"],t.s)
B.baN=new A.cN("audience",B.dR,"Who can hear my song?","Open the song, press Tools, then Share and who can hear it. The row Who can hear this has the answer beside it, and tapping it shows the whole picture:\n\n\u2022 Only you \u2014 nobody else is in the room it lives in\n\u2022 Your room \u2014 everybody in that room\n\u2022 People you asked \u2014 somebody invited to this one song\n\u2022 Anyone \u2014 it is on the Open Mic\n\nYou can move it back down at any time, and a take you have not shared stays private no matter where the song sits.",B.c9Z)
B.ewu=s(["song_audience_dial","audience_open_mic_toggle"],t.s)
B.cz8=s(["open","mic","publish","post","share","public","everybody","upload","showcase","song"],t.s)
B.baC=new A.cN("openmic",B.lQ,"How do I put a song on the Open Mic?",'Open the song, press Tools, then Share and who can hear it, then Who can hear this, and "Put it on the Open Mic".\n\nAny adult signed in can then find it, listen, and offer to play on it. Only the takes your room has already heard become audible \u2014 never one you are still working on privately. The same row takes it back down whenever you like.\n\nWhoever started a song is the one who puts it up. On a song somebody else started, the same row says who that is.',B.cz8)
B.cE7=s(["take","off","remove","delete","down","unpublish","hide","undo","mic","song"],t.s)
B.ba6=new A.cN("takedown",B.lQ,"How do I take a song off the Open Mic?",'Open the song, press Tools, then Share and who can hear it, then Who can hear this, and "Take it off the Open Mic". It stops being findable immediately.\n\nNothing you did while it was up is lost \u2014 the song, the takes and the song sheet all stay exactly as they were.\n\nWhoever started the song can take it down, and so can the room\u2019s owner.',B.cE7)
B.ewz=s(["/openmic","/openmic/musicians","ask_song_send","open_mic_ask_somebody_not_here"],t.s)
B.crX=s(["ask","help","request","collaborate","collaborator","musician","find","bass","drummer","singer","song"],t.s)
B.bab=new A.cN("ask",B.dR,"How do I ask somebody for help on a song?",'It depends on whether you have somebody in mind, and whether they are on the app.\n\nIf they are: on the Open Mic, tap them among the people there (More, then Narrow it down, finds them by what they play), and ask them from their page. They see the one song you named and nothing else of yours until they say yes.\n\nIf they are not on the app yet: on the Open Mic, tap More, then "Invite someone you know". It writes a message about one of your songs for you to send them, and it opens that one song to them, nothing else of yours.\n\nIf you have nobody in mind: put the song on the Open Mic and say what it needs. It then shows up for people who play that part, and they can offer.',B.crX)
B.ewb=s(["/notifications","ask_card_reply"],t.s)
B.caM=s(["asked","invite","invited","invitation","notification","bell","accept","decline","yes","request","join","song"],t.s)
B.b9T=new A.cN("answer-ask",B.dR,"Somebody asked me to play on their song. Where is it?","In your notifications \u2014 the bell in the top corner. Open it and you can say yes or no.\n\nSaying yes gives you that one song, not the rest of their work. Saying no tells them and nothing else happens.",B.caM)
B.ewy=s(["songs_new_room","your_music_tab_rooms"],t.s)
B.c6N=s(["room","rooms","band","group","folder","catalog","organise","organize","make","create","new"],t.s)
B.baa=new A.cN("rooms",B.ha,"What is a room, and how do I make one?","A room is who can see a set of songs \u2014 your band, a side project, or just the songs you write on your own. Every song lives in one, and the room decides who hears it.\n\nYour rooms are under Rooms, beside Songs and Sets, under the title of Your music. Make one there: press More, then New room. Your first song goes into Ideas, your own room, without asking; after that More, then New song, asks where it goes and can make the room on the way.",B.c6N)
B.ewW=s(["roomthread_more_invite","invite_link"],t.s)
B.ce5=s(["invite","add","member","bandmate","friend","room","join","collaborator","people"],t.s)
B.b9R=new A.cN("invite-room",B.ha,"How do I invite somebody to my room?","Open the room and tap Invite, beside the names under its title. Pick one of your people, or Send a link, or Show a code.\n\nA room invitation is everything in it, now and later \u2014 so if you only want somebody on one song, ask them to play on that song instead. You can also invite somebody you met on the Open Mic straight from their profile. In Messages, the room's conversation has it too: Tools, Members, then Invite somebody, to pick from your people or share a link.",B.ce5)
B.exv=s(["roomthread_more_members"],t.s)
B.cw0=s(["remove","kick","member","leave","left","quit","band","delete","room"],t.s)
B.baK=new A.cN("remove-member",B.ha,"How do I remove somebody from a room?","Open the room, then the members list, and remove them there. They lose the room and every song in it.\n\nWhat they already recorded stays \u2014 a take keeps its author, and removing somebody does not erase the work they did with you.",B.cw0)
B.ewk=s(["/account","open_mic_list_me"],t.s)
B.c8o=s(["sounds","like","genre","style","taste","tags","profile","describe","match","matching"],t.s)
B.bao=new A.cN("sounds-like",B.lQ,'What does "sounds like" do on my profile?','It is how the app finds people making the kind of music you make. "Guitarist" does not say whether you play metal or jazz; this does.\n\nNobody is ranked by it. It moves you sideways towards people in the same corner, never up or down past anybody. Set it on your page: on Account, tap your name, then Edit your page, then What you sound like. Five words at most \u2014 fewer and sharper works better than listing everything.',B.c8o)
B.ew9=s(["/account","open_mic_more_listed","open_mic_list_me"],t.s)
B.bE2=s(["discoverable","found","find","visible","hidden","profile","appear","listed","city","location","search","open","mic","showing"],t.s)
B.b9W=new A.cN("discoverable",B.lQ,"How do I show up in the Open Mic, or stop showing up?","On the Open Mic, tap More, then Listed on the Open Mic, pick one, and press the button under it. Or Account \u2192 Privacy and safety \u2192 Listed on the Open Mic, which asks the same way. It is off until you turn it on \u2014 nobody appears in the Open Mic without choosing to.\n\nThe same page has Who sees your city: nobody, only people you have made music with, or anybody browsing.",B.bE2)
B.ewx=s(["/openmic","/openmic/notes","/openmic/musicians","open_mic_leave_want","leave_want_your_notes","leave_want_send","yourpage_more_your_notes","/account","account_your_notes_row"],t.s)
B.ca5=s(["told","looking","joins","wanted","notes","left","turned"],t.s)
B.ba9=new A.cN("leave-a-note",B.lQ,"Can I be told when somebody I am looking for joins?",'Yes. On the Open Mic, tap More, then Notes, then "Leave a note for someone here". From Narrow it down it is at the top of the list however many people your search found. Choose who you would like to meet (if you searched for one kind of player they are already chosen), add a line for yourself if you like, and leave it.\n\nWhen somebody who plays that lists themselves on the Open Mic, you get a notification with their name, and tapping it opens their page. If you both show a town it has to be the same town, spelled the same way apart from capitals; if either of you shows none, the town does not come into it. Nobody is told who left a note.\n\nA note lasts a month. "Your notes", at the foot of the same sheet, is where you change one or take it down. It is in Account too, in More on Privacy and safety, as "Notes you left on the Open Mic", and in More on your page.',B.ca5)
B.ew6=s(["songs_new_set","your_music_tab_sets","play_the_set","share_set_pdf","the_bands_sets","give_set_to_room","live_previous_in_set","live_running_order","set_carry_on"],t.s)
B.ck_=s(["set","sets","setlist","setlists","list","gig","order","practice","performance","live","dep","sub","chart","key","tempo","form","ending","play","long","length","duration","minutes","slot","print","pdf","share","make","give","bandmates"],t.s)
B.ba1=new A.cN("sets",B.dR,"How do I make a set list?","In Your music, press More, then New set: name it, choose where it lives and, if you like, the day it is for, then press Make the set. Your sets are under Sets, beside Songs and Rooms.\n\nA set is a running order for one occasion \u2014 Friday practice, Saturday's show \u2014 built from songs you already have, in whatever order you will play them.\n\nEach row carries the key you do it in, the tempo, the count-in, the form, how it ends and a note. Key and notes on the row opens all six. Leave a field empty and the set uses what the song says.\n\nPlay this set walks the running order one song at a time, in the set's keys, with its tempo and notes on the stand, Previous and Next, and the recording off. Play from here starts part way down; leave a song early and Carry on takes you back to it.\n\nThe set adds up how long it runs. A length it measured from a recording and one it is working out are shown differently, and the total says how many of them are guesses. A song with nothing to go on has no length and is left out. A song whose sheet your phone has not been able to read says that instead, and the total says how many are still missing. The time between songs is never counted.\n\nHand this out gives you the three ways out of the app: print it, send the pack as a PDF with a chord chart for every song in the keys you play them in, or send the running order as text.\n\nA set can be the whole band\u2019s. Open the room: The band\u2019s sets is beside its songs. Everybody in the room sees the same running order, keys and notes on their own phone, and the room\u2019s owner and everybody who can record and edit can change it. The set says who changed it last, and never who opened it. When you open it, it fetches the latest and says what changed since your phone last had it; with no signal it shows the copy on your phone and says from when.\n\nTo make one of your own sets the band\u2019s, open it and press Give this set to the room. Every song in it has to be one of that room\u2019s songs first. From then on it is the room\u2019s: only the room\u2019s owner, or somebody who can record and edit, can give it back, from the set\u2019s Tools, under Finish, rename or delete, where the day it is for and Delete this set are too.",B.ck_)
B.exp=s(["live_recording"],t.s)
B.cpa=s(["silent","speaker","playback","backing","loud"],t.s)
B.baA=new A.cN("perform-silent",B.dR,"Can Perform be silent, with nothing coming out of the speaker?","Yes. In Perform, the switch beside Start says Recording on or Recording off; tap it. With the recording off nothing comes out of the phone, and the words still move in time with the song \u2014 the count-in, the beat you feel and the chords called out loud all carry on. Your phone remembers it.\n\nA set opens with the recording off, so on a stage only the words move, and your phone remembers what you choose for sets separately.",B.cpa)
B.exy=s(["song_keep_here","keep_set_here"],t.s)
B.cqN=s(["offline","signal","airplane","aeroplane","wifi","internet","reception","basement","van","kept","song","perform","phone","keep"],t.s)
B.b9Y=new A.cN("offline",B.kV,"Can I play a song where there is no signal?","Yes, if you keep it on your phone first. Open the song, press Tools, then Finish, rename or delete, and turn on Keep on this phone. A set has Keep on this phone in its Tools, and keeps every song in it \u2014 it says how much space that will take before it takes it, and once the day a set was for has passed it offers to take those songs back off.\n\nThat fetches the words, the song sheet, the recording and its separated parts, so Perform plays the song with its chords and beats with no connection at all. The switch is then on, and a small phone sits beside the name of the song; turn the switch off to take the song off.\n\nIf the app cannot open because there is no signal, the songs you kept are listed on that screen, ready to perform, and so are the sets you have opened on this phone, as this phone last had them, ready to play in order.\n\nIt is only for you and only on this phone: nobody in the room is told, and nobody else who signs in here sees them. A song that is not kept still opens with its words, and says that the recording is missing. In a browser there is nowhere to keep a song, so Tools does not offer it there.",B.cqN)
